# THE FUSIONS THAT OWE NO EQUALITY BECAUSE THE OVERLAP WAS FOUND AND COULD NOT BE SIZED. One
# row per composed layer that FILES a demand elimination whose quantity is `unmeasured`.
#
# ⭐⭐ THIS IS A DIFFERENT DOCUMENT FROM AN UNSEARCHED ONE AND IT SUSPENDS FOR A DIFFERENT
#    REASON. "We know these hours are double counted and cannot say by how much" is a
#    composer who looked, found something, and reported the honest width of their ignorance.
#    Reading that as a zero -- which `coalesce(e.low, 0)` does -- asserts a sum the composer
#    explicitly declined to make.
#
# ⛔ SO THE SUSPENSION HAS GROUNDS AT MORE THAN ONE LEVEL, and a checker that handles only the
#   first is right about three fusions and wrong about the fourth. They are separate files so
#   each can be run and counted alone, and united in composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc so no
#   caller has to remember them. ⚠️ THAT UNION IS A BAG: one fusion can be suspended on more
#   than one ground and is suspended once, which is why composition/suspended_fusions.sqlc
#   exists as the projection and why a third ground once turned fourteen fusions into
#   seventeen rows.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ IT CARRIES `quantity` RATHER THAN PINNING IT, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES IT COMPOSABLE. An
#    elimination is filed PER QUANTITY (pm.elimination's key is composition, composed layer,
#    quantity) and this relation used to filter `quantity = 'demand'` and drop the column. Its
#    union then wore the name "the composed layers that owe no sum AT ALL" while suspending only
#    the demand sum, so the first nameplate rule to compose it would have been wrong in BOTH
#    directions: suspended because the DEMAND elimination was unsized, and letting a nameplate
#    elimination filed `unmeasured` through into a `coalesce(..., 0)`. A caller now says which
#    grain it means.
#
# ⭐⭐ AND IT SUSPENDS ON ANY TYPED ABSENCE, NOT ONLY `unmeasured`. An elimination quantity is a
#    `pm:StatedClaim`, so its absent branch is a `pm:ClaimAbsence` carrying
#    `pm:ClaimAbsenceReason` -- {unmeasured, notApplicable, derived}, with `none` NOT in the type.
#    Filtering to `unmeasured` left the other two to survive owed_equality and be read as the
#    NUMBER ZERO. tests/composition.rs returns `None` on any typed absence; the two witnesses
#    stated different rules and nothing said so.
-- eliminations/filed.sqlc wherever asrt:quantity takes its pm:absent branch, per quantity.
SELECT e.composition, e.composed_layer, e.quantity,
       'the overlap was found and could not be sized' AS suspended_because,
       e.reason AS note
FROM (
    :compose(eliminations/filed.sqlc)
) e
WHERE e.absent IS NOT NULL
